<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jin Shuren</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1879">1879</a>–<a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jin Shuren was a Chinese official who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a> from 1928, after the assassination of Yang Zengxin, until 1933. His abolition of the Kumul Khanate in 1930, heavy taxes and settlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-chinese">Han Chinese</a> provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumul-rebellion">Kumul Rebellion</a>, which spread across the province and drew in the Hui warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ma-zhongying">Ma Zhongying</a>. He was overthrown in a coup in April 1933 and fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> proper.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jin-shuren.jpg" alt="Jin Shuren" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jin_Shuren_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
